cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "locallm: small language models trained only on code seven proof systems agree is correct"
message: "If you refer to this work, cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cuzzort
    given-names: Treston Malachi
repository-code: "https://github.com/trestoncuzzort/locallm"
abstract: >-
  A pipeline that keeps a generated program as training data only when it passes its tests, is proven against
  its specification by Dafny, Verus, SPARK, Frama-C, Lean 4, Rocq and F*, and has a deliberately broken copy of
  itself refuted by all seven at a concrete input. Includes the t specification language and its seven
  lowerings, the grading harness, the measured coverage and agreement tables, and tup, a Linux distribution
  built from source with a receipt for every step.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - synthetic data
  - program synthesis
  - small language models
license-url: "https://github.com/trestoncuzzort/locallm/blob/main/LICENSE"
